<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27292" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŭto</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a.
		2. lutum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to bedaub with mud</i> or <i>clay</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R.
			92</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nidosque reversa lutabit hirundo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Calp.
					Ecl. 5, 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lutati tituli statuarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lampr. Elag. 14</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to bedaub,
			besmear</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ne lutet immundum nitidos ceroma capillos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 14, 50, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crassis lutatus amomis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pers.
					3, 104</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
